//? Title: MD5 as a reproducible checksum study
//? Subtitle: Actual padding, modular compression states and the original72 bit flips
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A byte-string checksum maps arbitrary input to a fixed-size digest. This study
reproduces MD5’s published test vectors and exposes actual padding, decoded
blocks, modular steps and feed-forward states from the canonical native
producer. We retain the original nine-byte avalanche example and distinguish
finite diffusion observations from collision resistance, which MD5 does not
provide.
)

\toc

> From bytes to modular steps

MD5 pads a message with a one bit, zeros and a64-bit little-endian original
length modulo2^64, forming64-byte blocks. Decode each block into sixteen
little-endian uint32 words. Four working words start from the incoming chaining
state. Each of64 steps applies its prescribed Boolean function, adds a selected
word and constant modulo2^32, rotates, adds the old b word, and permutes the
working positions. Feed-forward adds the final working words into the incoming
chain modulo2^32.

The canonical producer uses defined unsigned modular arithmetic. Its trace
captures actual before/after words and actual decoded bytes, without
implementing a second explanatory hash. The report is a checksum/mechanism
study: diffusion on chosen inputs cannot establish collision resistance, and
MD5’s known collision weakness excludes using it where that property is
required.

> A tiny actual first step

For the three bytes abc, the first actual decoded word is0x80636261: a,b,c
followed by the padding byte0x80 in little-endian order. The diagram reads the
real first step’s modular sum and rotated value. The printed digest is the
actual canonical output.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md5_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/md5.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::md5_trace("abc");
    auto &s = t.steps.front();
    std::print("Actual canonical digest: `{}`.\n\n| actual step observation | hexadecimal value |\n| --- | " "--- |\n| selected decoded word | 0x{:08x} |\n| Boolean function | 0x{:08x} |\n| additive " "constant | 0x{:08x} |\n| modular sum | 0x{:08x} |\n| rotated word | 0x{:08x} |\n| new b | " "0x{:08x} |\n",
               dm::algorithms::to_hex(t.analysis.digest), s.word, s.function,
               s.constant, s.sum, s.rotated, s.after[1]);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("word", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual decoded word{}\n0x{:08x}", s.word_index, s.word)).node("sum", {6, 0}, std::format("Actual modular sum\n0x{:08x}", s.sum)).node("rotate", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual rotate left {}\n0x{:08x}", s.shift, s.rotated)).edge("word", "sum").edge("sum", "rotate");
    d.save_svg("build/md5_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
