> Published vectors and the original avalanche experiment

The native reference-vector helper retains all seven fixed published expected
digests. The program computes each actual digest before comparing it with the
expected value. The original baseline word avalanche contains nine bytes,
giving72 distinct single-input-bit mutations; the legacy prose called it eight
bytes while its loop already performed72 flips.

The native study hashes the baseline and each real mutant, then counts actual
output-bit differences. Display every mutation outcome directly, without
clipping outlying counts into edge histogram bins. The horizontal64-bit
reference is half of the128-bit digest width. A finite mean near that reference
is descriptive; it neither proves independent output bits nor excludes chosen
collisions.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md5_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/md5.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::print("| RFC vector | actual message bytes | actual digest | equals published expected |\n| ---: | " "---: | --- | --- |\n");
    std::size_t index = 0;
    for (auto & [message, expected] : dm::algorithms::md5_reference_vectors()) {
        auto actual = dm::algorithms::md5_hex(message);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", index++, message.size(), actual,
                   actual == expected);
    }
    auto a = dm::algorithms::md5_avalanche(dm::algorithms::md5_demo_message());
    std::print("\nActual flips {}; measured mean {:.12f}; minimum {}; maximum {}.\n",
               a.flips.size(), a.mean_changed, a.minimum_changed,
               a.maximum_changed);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    for (auto &f : a.flips) {
        x.push_back(f.bit);
        y.push_back(f.changed);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual digest changes");
    p.abline_h(64, {220, 38, 38}, 1.5).y_limits(0, 128).x_label(
        "actual flipped input bit, byte-major LSB first").y_label(
        "actual differing digest bits out of128").title("Original nine-byte baseline: all72 actual mutations").save_svg("build/md5_original.svg");
}
```
