> Inspect actual working-state changes

The next figure counts differing bits between each step’s actual
before/after128-bit working state for abc. This includes the specified
permutation of a,b,c,d as well as the new b value. It is a trajectory of one
execution, not the output avalanche study and not an experiment about the digest
of truncated rounds. Feed-forward is recorded separately at each block boundary.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md5_steps.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/md5.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::md5_trace("abc");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual step | selected word index | actual state changed bits |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps) {
        auto changed = dm::algorithms::md5_state_hamming(s.before, s.after);
        x.push_back(s.index);
        y.push_back(changed);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index, s.word_index, changed);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "actual state changes");
    p.x_label("actual step in the single abc block").y_label(
        "actual before/after state Hamming distance").title(
        "Actual working-state trajectory, including permutation").save_svg(
        "build/md5_steps.svg");
}
```
