> Padding boundaries, work and capture

The empty message still requires a padding block. Length55 fits its suffix in
one block; length56 needs two. Complete padded-size geometry is checked before
copying or appending. The input length encoding deliberately retains RFC
modulo2^64 bit semantics; container geometry is checked separately rather than
confused with that modular field.

For N input bytes and B padded blocks, canonical hashing performs64B steps and
uses O(N) padded workspace. It is not a streaming API. The avalanche study
hashes8N mutants after copying their N-byte messages, giving O(N^2) work plus
O(N) outcome records. Its optional complete mutation-count cap defaults to one
million, with zero disabling it. Empty studies retain the actual empty-message
digest and no outcomes; mean/min/max zero values are explicitly placeholders.

Complete trace admission counts N original bytes, P padded bytes,65 records per
block and16 final digest bytes. Default limit is one million logical entries;
zero disables that optional cap. Record fields, capacities, runtime copies and
payload bytes within record fields are excluded from that logical count.
Captured storage has a larger constant than the count suggests. Complete
geometry/admission checks precede copying/padding, and a failure never returns a
partial history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/md5_padding.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/md5.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| prescribed input bytes | actual padded bytes | actual blocks | actual steps | complete " "capture entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {0, 1, 55, 56, 63, 64, 119, 120}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::md5_trace(std::string(n, 'a'));
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(t.analysis.blocks);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, t.analysis.padded_bytes,
                   t.analysis.blocks, t.analysis.steps, t.captured_entries);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual padded blocks");
    p.x_label("prescribed message byte count").y_label("actual64-byte compression blocks").title("Real padding boundaries change block counts").save_svg("build/md5_padding.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
