| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 64 | 1 | 64 | 145 |
| 1 | 64 | 1 | 64 | 146 |
| 55 | 64 | 1 | 64 | 200 |
| 56 | 128 | 2 | 128 | 330 |
| 63 | 128 | 2 | 128 | 337 |
| 64 | 128 | 2 | 128 | 338 |
| 119 | 128 | 2 | 128 | 393 |
| 120 | 192 | 3 | 192 | 523 |
\image(figures/md5_padding.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual padded block/step counts around boundary lengths.)
\alttext(Empty input has one block; the length56 and120 boundaries each need an additional block.)

> Verification and references

Native tests retain all seven RFC expected digests and inspect actual padding,
decoded words, every Boolean function/word selection/modular sum/rotation/state
update and each feed-forward for every byte length0..256 with arbitrary bytes.
Test constants are independently evaluated from the published sine formula.
Every original mutation is rehashed and bit-counted independently, with exact
means/min/max, empty behavior, binary NUL/high bytes, ownership and quota
boundaries. The shared ten-report batch passes 71 CTest cases, 29 directly
instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 130 compiled and executed public examples,
598/598 scoped documentation definitions and ten representative hovers.
Independent Python arbitrary-precision, hashlib, sorted-window, RNG, polynomial,
graph and full-assignment references verify 224,229 actual records. Frozen
comparisons preserve ordinary legacy outputs, including selected clique
identities, original density graphs and memetic partitions. Twelve checkout
headers and twelve identically installed headers compile independently; an
installed-header native consumer links and runs. All four complete programs and
all four native figures pass execution and visual review, and HTML/Markdown
exports preserve computed results and identical image bytes. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-224-233/`.

[RFC1321|https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1321] specifies the algorithm and
reference vectors. [RFC6151|https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6151] updates its
security considerations and explains the collision-resistance limitation. No
diffusion plot in this report overrides that limitation.
